  "diagnosis": {
    "concrete_gap": "E6 generated close poses remain precise, but the learned policy closes 18 steps earlier with much worse wrist heading/lateral alignment; acquisition falls before transport. The gap is policy attainment of the demonstrated aligned pre-close state, not source-pose precision.",
    "evidence": [
      "First near-close: E6 176 vs E2 167, so the acquisition loss is not explained by fewer close opportunities.",
      "All-near heading median 2.982 -> 8.158 deg; gap has same sign in all four |yaw| strata.",
      "All-near XY offset median 12.739 -> 18.412 mm.",
      "First acquisition 78/167 -> 48/176; first-failed grasp increased 89 -> 128.",
      "Generated first-close XY/heading precision is essentially unchanged (E2 3.705 mm/0.714 deg; E6 3.337 mm/0.717 deg), so worse rollout alignment is not inherited from worse generated close poses."
    ],
    "first_failed_milestone": "grasp acquisition (first near-close occurs, but the 40-step secured criterion is not reached)",
    "height_conclusion": "The all-near close-height medians are similar and E6 is slightly higher, so the -5 mm generated offset did not transfer to policy rollout height.",
    "recommendation": {
      "caution": "This is post-hoc and may still fail: E1 showed that heading improvement alone need not raise success. H5 should be rejected unless acquisition and performance improve under frozen criteria.",
      "concrete_intervention": "Starting from the stock E2 natural60 generation path (no Z offset), repeat the final already-aligned open-gripper waypoint for one preregistered fixed dwell duration immediately before the first close; leave pose geometry, source selection/pool, close/lift/place segments, generated count, BC, and evaluation unchanged.",
      "proceed_with_H5": true,
      "required_preregistration_gate": "Freeze one dwell duration before generation. Require generated first-close XY/heading/height to remain within a narrow preregistered tolerance of E2 and the dwell count to be exact; after training, require later first-near-close timing plus lower all-near heading/XY error and higher first-secured fraction versus E2 before interpreting performance.",
      "single_factor": "fixed open-gripper alignment dwell immediately before the first close in every generated demonstration",
      "why_single_factor": "Only the number of repeated pre-close alignment samples changes. This directly reweights the demonstrated state-action region the policy fails to attain without modifying positions, headings, close height, or lift timing after close."
    }
  },
